  "progression": [
    "The first year comprises twelve 5 EC courses. Optics and Mammalian Cell Biology accompany the practical in 1a. Calculus, Organic Chemistry 1 and Biochemistry in 1b precede Thermodynamics in 2a; Cell Biology also precedes Physiology. Scientific Reading and Communication and Biophysics come later.",
    "The second year comprises twelve 5 EC courses. First-year chemistry, thermodynamics and biological foundations precede Applied Microbiology and its linked practical. Calculus and Optics precede mechanics. Spectroscopic Tools in 1b precedes Imaging in 2a. The organic chemistry practical accompanies the second organic chemistry course. Genetics and Biotechnology in 2b build on first-year molecular genetics and biochemistry.",
    "Complete the first two years for 120 EC before the research project. Its condition also requires completion of every first-year course. The Board of Examiners approves the electives and project; electives have course-specific requirements. The elective areas and optional focus packages do not constitute separate majors. A 30 EC minor remains separate, with external minors requiring approval. Future scheduling is subject to the applicable catalogue."
  ]
